  "description": "kube-controller-manager leadership and controller work queues. Custom dashboard (the Kubernetes project publishes none); metric families verified against kubernetes v1.37.1 sources: workqueue_depth, workqueue_adds_total, workqueue_queue_duration_seconds, workqueue_work_duration_seconds, workqueue_retries_total (component-base/metrics/prometheus/workqueue), plus the standard process_ collectors. Leadership comes from kube-state-metrics' kube_lease_owner for the kube-controller-manager Lease (k3s registers no leader_election_master_status). k3s runs the component inside the k3s server process: the kube-controller-manager ScrapeConfig (apps/kube-control-plane) scrapes every node and keeps only these families, so process_* describe the whole k3s process and the work queues include the API server's and k3s's own controllers (told apart by the queue name). API client request counts are left out: the k3s process shares one REST-client registry across every component.",
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
